<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109830" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφέλκ-ω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>draw away under, draw away underhand</i> or <i>gently,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. [τινὰ] ποδοῖιν</span>
			<i>draw</i> one <i>away</i> by the two feet, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				14.477
			</span></i>; <i>draw away by undermining,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. παρὰ σφᾶς τὸν χοῦν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					2.76
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				66.4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. κάτωθεν τὸ κλιμάκιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.781e
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. τοὺς πόδας,</span> i.e. to be
			slippery, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.187
			</span></i>: —
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περσικὰς ὑφέλκομαι</span>
			<i>I trail</i> Persian slippers <i>under my feet,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				319
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑφελκέσθω τὸ ὑποπόδιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Heliod.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				49.8.19
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
